 2. 🚦 Smarter traffic lights 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Nashville has 200+ lidar sensors monitoring traffic, without the privacy concerns of license plate-reading cameras. Image: Ouster Laser-sensing technology is being paired with AI to make traffic lights smarter, Axios' Joann Muller reports. 

 Smart traffic lights can give slower pedestrians more time to cross, or keep cars moving when nobody's waiting. 🚙 Driving the news: Nashville is expanding its deployment of lidar-based traffic technology from Ouster, adding 100 intersections to an existing network.

 Ouster's BlueCity system uses lidar sensors to create detailed 3D images of traffic movements, which AI software analyzes in real time. 📷 The system can detect movement up to 500 feet away and capture color information, letting it distinguish between traffic signal colors. 

