 4. 📸 Pic to go: Shuttle stands 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: David Swanson/AFP via Getty Images L.A.'s Samuel Oschin Air and Space Center recently began welcoming visitors to one of the world's most impressive displays of science history: NASA's Space Shuttle Endeavour, vertically stacked as if taking off.

 Former astronaut Garrett Reisman told Space.com of the nearly 200-foot-tall display: "It just takes your breath away when you see that reveal and the doors open and you get to look at it for the first time." 🚀 Endeavour was built to replace Challenger. It last flew in 2011.

 It's now one of four orbiters and test shuttles on display nationwide. See the exhibit . 

 
 
